            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0754" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-10T09:00:00-04:00">September 10, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Presidential decree places all Paraguay in state of siege for period of 2
                    months starting September 9. All quiet but uneasiness still evident.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
